<<~ &#x0002; >>

<<~ ahu #head >>

! `hoʻokupu` ~ the flow that cannot become an estate

> ''PROVISIONAL.'' The shape below carries measured findings and no code.

`hoʻokupu` — an offering ''laid down at a place'', etymologically //to cause growth//. It rhymes structurally with `hoʻokipa`: two `hoʻo-` causatives, hospitality and offering, the two halves of what a guest and a host do to each other.

''A flow REFILLS; a stock ACCUMULATES.'' The distinction is not stylistic. Roman law records it: obligations //of the nature of money or money's worth// ''passed to the heirs like property'', while unpriced personal obligations ''died with the person''. ''Pricing and transferability convert a relation into a heritable estate'' — which is the freezing mechanism, adopted as the cure.

''So the medium refuses three properties'': it does not accumulate (the refresh ''discards'' the unspent remainder — carry-forward IS stock), it does not transfer between holders (you spend it ''on'' someone's contribution, never give it ''to'' them), and it carries no running total.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #the-refutation >>

!! The giver-bound hypothesis — REFUTED, three times

''The design's central mechanism was wrong and the correction is measured.'' Bounding each giver's expiring allowance was expected to bound concentration. It does not:

* a system capping every giver's votes daily runs ''Gini 0.976 on reputation received'', top 1% at 67.9%
* another reads ''0.59 out → 0.94 in''
* a third's moderators come out flat

''Both low-concentration systems bound the RECEIVER instead'' — one hard-caps the score at [−1,+5] and runs Gini 0.30; another allows one approval per project per voter and runs ~0.41. ''The receiver-side cap is the only lever with any measured success behind it.''

And cumulative advantage runs on ''prestige, not merit'', proven under randomisation: seeding ONE award to randomly-chosen contributors produced 12/100 further awards against 2/100 controls, with //no greater productivity//. ''One gift begets six.''

''Do not render running totals.'' The count carries the concentration; the act does not.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #open >>

!! Open

* ''Anonymity costs half the volume'' (−50% to −59% measured) and cures ''retaliation locks'', never concentration. Three attention kinds ride the three identity layers — passive trace (`maka`) · anonymous offering · Handle-attested offering — and publicity reads ''scale-relative'': named at your layer, anonymous one rung out.
* ''Recognition aimed at the periphery can EXPEL it'' — unfloored rewards drove less-active contributors away, while a quality floor followed by RANDOM allocation held them (+20% retention at month one, +13% at quarter four). ''Floor, then lottery.''
* The receiver-side cap may already ride the emoji form: one glyph per person per post is a per-recipient saturation nobody chose for that reason.
* ''Prior art, and how it died'': demurrage currencies solved hoarding and left transferability intact — a leaking estate stays an estate — and one such scheme was shut by a national bank, which is categorisation risk in its plainest form.

